WEBVTT

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:11.400
"Kodomo no Odocha"

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:13.740
That rumor that I love you

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:17.370
is true, yes it is.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:20.870
You can't ignore it either.

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:25.460
Whether you're awake or asleep,

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:29.090
please don't be embarrassed.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.680
Is it a sin if I sneak into your heart

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:40.350
by ridding you...

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:43.520
...of your other love?

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:48.110
At sunset,

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:50.610
when the children go home,

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:54.530
Today's incident is burning love!

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:58.450
You can tell it accurately.

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:00.540
7 O'Clock News!

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:04.330
Please, our relationship...

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:09.960
Please don't blame it on the true kiss

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:11.800
In a city without light,

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:15.680
let's burn the fire of love.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.100
Don't be so easy going

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:21.390
The existence is a mistake

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:24.890
You're asking for something not there.

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:35.650
I'm Kurata Sana, a 6th grader
and TV personality.

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:38.660
My beloved Mama is an
Aoki-award winning novelist.

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:41.950
My chauffeur, manager,
and former boyfriend Rei-kun.

00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:44.000
The mysterious white bat straight man.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:45.660
I'm Babbit!

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:48.670
My natural enemy and good friend,
Hayama Akito.

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:51.670
And this is Jinbo Elementary School's
disciplinarian, Andoh-sensei.

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:52.880
I'm Andoh!

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:57.380
"Math Life Drives Me Batty"

00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:00.390
--Good morning.

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:03.720
Kurata Sana...

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:05.060
What!? What!?

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:07.230
Has Sana-chan suddenly
found herself in a pinch!?

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.060
Akito-kun,

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:14.070
we can't have any fighting.
Wait here, and let's see what happens.

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:17.070
Who are you, Mito Komon?

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:19.070
It's really Sana-chan!

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:19.740
Sign this?

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:21.740
Sure.

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:23.200
Ah, thank goodness!

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:26.410
If you had said you couldn't sign anything
for some scary middle-school girls,

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:28.080
I don't know what I would do!

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:29.420
Me too, me too!

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:32.380
Nah, my fans are important to me.

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:34.670
Speaking of which, Sana-chan, what are
you going to do about middle school?

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:37.050
Naturally, you're coming up
through our middle school, right?

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:42.430
That's right... I hadn't realized it,
but I'm going to be in middle school soon.

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:44.100
Sana-chan, it's still only September.

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:44.180
"That's still a long way off..."

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:47.350
Yeah, that's right! Middle school!

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:49.060
Hmph. Aren't you happy-go-lucky?

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:51.400
Listen, Hayama, young man!

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:56.360
Why are you laughing at everyone else's
positive attitude towards life!?

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:58.740
That's right, it's no use
trying to talk to him.

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:00.610
If talking to him won't work, I'll sing!

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:00.660
"A song is a message of the heart"

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:03.410
What happened to you two?

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:05.910
--Okay, let's go, Hayama!
We're going to think positive,
--Huh, me too?

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:07.080
--peel some skin,
and find forte and foible!
--What's going on here!?

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:10.290
Let's come-come over the rainbow!

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:15.420
♪ Let's go, let's go,
to fun, fun, middle school! ♪

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:19.470
♪ Those cute uniforms
are a little embarrassing. ♪

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:23.090
Sana-chan...

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:24.720
What are you talking about, Scarecrow?

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:26.390
S- Sea--?

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:30.770
There's a bright, enjoyable
middle-school life waiting ahead for us.

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:32.020
That's six months away.

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:35.020
Yes. The road you must
go down is endlessly long.

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:36.360
What is this, a folk song?

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:38.030
It won't be many more nights
until New Year's!

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:39.690
After that, middle school
is nearly upon us!

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:42.360
Let's go junior high school!

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:54.380
Children, good morning...

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:56.040
Sensei, what's the matter?

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:57.380
She's absolutely blue!

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:59.090
"Mitsuya-sensei's worries"

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:02.720
Children, please don't be
shocked when you hear this...

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:03.720
The truth is...

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:05.680
--Huh!? Flunk!?

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:05.720
"Everyone could flunk"

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:07.390
Sensei, how come!?

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:09.390
What do you mean, we might
not make it to middle school?

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:12.060
Madam, what on earth
are you talking about?

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:16.060
Our class is significantly
behind on the lesson plan, right?

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:17.610
You should basically be able
to go right into middle school

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:20.070
with this school's
escalator system, but...

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:21.070
But...?

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:26.070
Our class test average
is 15 points below the others.

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:28.410
We're starting to gain ground
on the lesson plan schedule,

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:30.330
but at the pace we're going,
it wouldn't be right

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:32.000
to let all of you pass
right on into middle school.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.330
Everyone should be tested
to check their aptitude,

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:38.670
in order to see what can be expected of
your efforts, according to Andoh-sensei.

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:40.000
A test!?

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.010
That's right!

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:44.760
A te---st!

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:48.010
A- Andoh-sensei, when did you get here?

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:50.680
I've been hiding
under the podium for a while.

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:52.020
Here's a visualization.

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:53.680
Listen up, everyone!

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:58.360
I always knew that 3rd Class
was a troublesome, awful class,

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:00.020
chock-full of serious problems!

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:03.690
Andoh-sensei, you don't
have to put it so harshly.

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:07.030
Mitsuya-sensei! In cases like this, it is
the way of the educator to deal harshly!

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:08.030
I'm sorry!

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:10.700
The test is in three days! Understood!?

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:12.080
"The test is in 3 days"

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:14.710
W- what does the principal
have to say about this?

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:17.040
Yeah! How is it that our principal
is going to stand for this!?

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:18.710
Be quiet!

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:22.050
The principal was good enough
to gladly give his approval to this.

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:24.840
The test is in three days.
Those who do not get passing grades

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:27.050
will not be allowed to
enter Jinbo Middle School.

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:28.720
Is that understood!?

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:32.640
And so, Sana-chan and the others
were made to take an aptitude test

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:35.350
on language, math, science,
and social studies.

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:37.850
Wow, the principal
gave his approval for this?

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:40.190
That man is pretty strict, huh?

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:45.360
For whatever I said, I really don't have
the principal's permission to do this.

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:47.030
You know, sometimes it's
necessary to tell a lie.

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:49.070
Are you okay with this, Principal!?

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:52.370
"The principal is
traveling on business!"

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:56.040
I couldn't help it. This lie is only
out of consideration for the students.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:57.710
Hold on, Aunt-- Big Sister...

00:05:57.710 --> 00:06:00.710
I'm sure those children resent me,
and despise me.

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:03.340
However... however... if I must,
I will play the ogre!

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:03.170
"Even ogres can be moved to tears"

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:06.720
But in my heart... in my heart,
I am an angel!

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:09.050
You've still got an ogre's face.

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:10.890
Your makeup fell off.

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:14.390
As a result,

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:18.060
starting today,
we will be staying after school.

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:21.230
Aah, this is lame. After-school class?

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:23.730
Whose fault is it that we're
behind in our lesson plan?

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:25.740
You boys have done nothing
but get in the way of our lessons.

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:27.280
Children, listen.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:30.110
Back then, I was quick
to burst into tears,

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:33.660
and you really couldn't count on me,
when I was supposed to be the teacher.

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:35.790
Which is why I want
to be the one to make sure

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:38.000
that all of you get into middle school!

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.670
I'll help, too!

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:42.080
Tanaka-sensei! But...

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:46.460
Sensei... Tanaka-sensei...!

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:51.680
You're sure about this, Tanaka-sensei?

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:53.010
Of course.

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:54.680
Thank you so much.

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:56.350
Mitsuya-sensei...

00:06:56.350 --> 00:06:57.350
Tanaka-sensei...

00:06:57.350 --> 00:06:58.350
Mitsuya-sensei...

00:06:58.350 --> 00:06:59.350
Tanaka-sensei...

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:00.350
Mitsuya-sensei...

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:01.350
Tanaka-sensei...

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:02.360
Mitsuya-sensei...

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:03.020
Tanaka-sensei...

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:05.360
Mitsuya-sensei...

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:06.690
"You're sure everything is all right?"

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:09.610
Okay then, let's start with math.

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:12.030
Everyone, please look
at the printout I just handed out.

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:14.030
Everything we have studied up
to now has been compiled on here.

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:17.700
If you don't know the formulas,
or how to solve anything, ask away.

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:19.370
Sensei!

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:20.710
Yes, Sugita-san?

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:23.710
Sana-chan has gone rigid.

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:26.710
I- I don't know any of this.

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:28.380
S- Sana-chan...

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:31.300
My head is spinning.
I think I'm going to throw up.

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:33.340
W- which part don't you understand?

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:36.350
I- I don't even know which parts
I don't understand.

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:38.020
Well, do you understand this?

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:40.020
I- it's not so much this, as all of it.

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:41.020
You don't understand?

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:41.690
Yeah.

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:42.980
S- Sana-chan...!

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:45.860
You see, my experience
with being poor at math goes way back,

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:48.360
and it would take a
long time to tell you about it.

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:50.240
I will explain it in song.

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:50.240
"Sana's Math Life"

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:54.700
♪ Remembering back to
when I was in first grade, ♪

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:56.660
♪ I skipped school to do commercials. ♪

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:58.660
♪ Whoopsie-daisy, I stumbled, ♪

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:00.710
♪ And in second grade, I fell flat. ♪

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:02.710
♪ In third grade, I took a tumble. ♪

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:04.710
♪ In fourth grade, I made a big splash. ♪

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:06.670
♪ Knowing this was bad,
and trying to climb back out, ♪

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:09.050
♪ I struggled and I struggled,
but even so, ♪

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:11.050
♪ Fifth grade math
came falling down on me, ♪

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:13.010
♪ and once again,
I was back in the crapper. ♪

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:15.010
♪ Glub-glub, I'm now in sixth grade, ♪

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:17.470
♪ wanting to go to a country
with no math. ♪

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:23.600
That's all. This has
been the substandard,

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:26.020
New Year's wreath,
cuckoo tale of Sana's math life.

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:29.400
T- thank you. Sana-chan...

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:30.360
Yes?

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:31.320
This is difficult for me to tell you...

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:32.990
What is it?

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:36.280
Chances are, you really could be
at risk for going to middle school.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:42.330
"Zenjiro's 'Child's Toy"

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:44.330
What!? You're gonna be held back!?

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:48.000
That's right. I'm pretty
sure of my language and stuff,

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:50.000
but I don't get math at all.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:54.010
Sana can't do math, and could be in
elementary school the rest of her life.

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:56.010
Aw, that is trouble.

00:08:56.010 --> 00:08:58.350
Hey, Sana-chan, that means
you'll be a regular on "Child's Toy"

00:08:58.350 --> 00:08:59.350
the rest of your life.

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:00.640
The rest of my life!?

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:05.440
"Zenjiro's Child's Toy, Part 70"

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:08.360
Good evening,
awl you good boys and goils.

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:14.030
"Sana-chan's 88th Birthday Celebration"

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:12.440
On tonight's "Child's Toy" we will be
commemuhrating Sana-chan's 88 years.

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:14.030
Congratulations, Sana-chan.

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:15.700
Yoo-hoo...!

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:18.030
No!! No! No! I want
to be in middle school!

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:21.040
--No! No! No! No! No!
--I wonduh how old I'll be then...

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:25.620
All right then, at this point,
this week's Sana-chan.

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:31.130
This is my fault.

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:35.300
--As your manager, Sana-chan,
if I had kept a closer eye on your math.
--Sensei! Your manuscript, please!

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:37.970
--It's not exactly your fault, Rei-kun.
--Sensei! Your manuscript!

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:40.300
Oh! I know!

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:44.310
If we need to, why don't
I take your test in your place?

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:46.310
See? Perfect!

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:48.310
There's nothing to worry about, you two.

00:09:48.310 --> 00:09:48.980
Sensei!

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:50.650
Middle school is part
of mandatory education.

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:51.610
Even if they don't

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:54.650
--let you into Jinbo Middle School,
you can always go to a public school.
--The only proper manuscript

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:55.650
--Public school?
--you've given me lately is
"The Adventures of Thunderboy"!

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:56.650
--That's right!
--you've given me lately is
"The Adventures of Thunderboy"!

00:09:56.650 --> 00:09:58.990
--Public schools have
some good things about them.
--Please! Ow-ow-ow-ow-ow!

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:03.330
Most importantly, Sana, you don't
have any reason to be famous anymore.

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:05.120
There's no need to be
in a private school,

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:07.330
which takes it easier
on someone in show business.

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:10.000
--That's right! I can just
go to public school!
--My feet are burning up!

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:11.790
Good for you, Sana-chan!

00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:15.880
That would mean being separated
from Aya-chan, Mami-chan,

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:19.010
Hisae-chan, Tsuyoshi-kun,
and Hayama, wouldn't it!?

00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:22.010
I have to study!

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:23.930
"Sana-chan sings"

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:23.930
But, before that,
you need a little boost!

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:27.020
What's so bad about math!?
(What's so bad about math!?)

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:30.350
♪ I sort of understand
addition and subtraction. ♪

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:33.650
♪ My multiplication
and division is hopeless. ♪

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:35.280
♪ --Decimals and fractions,
fraction multiplication, ♪
--What's so bad about math?

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:36.990
♪ --fraction division,
formulas and theorems! ♪
--What's so bad about math? Yay!

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:38.320
♪ --Base times height divided by two,
when dividing fractions, flip them over, ♪
--What's so bad about math?

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:39.990
♪ --Base times height divided by two,
when dividing fractions, flip them over, ♪
--What's so bad about math? Whoo!

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:40.990
♪ --And multiply them! ♪
--What's so bad about math?

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:42.320
♪ Distance divided by time,
time times speed! ♪
--What's so bad about math? Whoo!

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:44.660
♪ Pi is 3.14! ♪
--What's so bad about math?
What's so bad about math?

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:46.700
♪ What's so bad about math!? ♪
--What's so bad about math?

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:52.210
All right, here goes!

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:54.670
Hey...!

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:58.220
Sana-chan, excuse me... hey...!

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:28.040
No time for that! Study! Study! Study!

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:29.710
Sana-chan, amazing!

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:31.370
Did you study at home, too?

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:36.380
Yeah, well, I got hypnotized by the math,
and fell asleep, so now I'm panicking.

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:38.380
Guys, stand by me, okay? Okay? Okay?

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:40.050
It's okay, Sana-chan.

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:41.760
We're all going to
middle school together.

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:42.380
Let's hang together!

00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:45.720
Mm-hmm! Thanks! That's real friendship!

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:48.390
Friendship! Isn't that
a nice word, Akito-kun?

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:51.060
Say, Akito-kun,
let's both help Sana-chan, too!

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:52.060
Doing what?

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:54.900
Why, helping her study, of course!

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:56.070
Starting with the small things,
and then building up--

00:11:56.070 --> 00:11:57.730
Won't do any good.

00:11:57.730 --> 00:11:59.400
It's hopeless.

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:03.410
She can't do anything about her math,
no matter what we try.

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:06.410
Akito-kun, what did you just say?

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:07.740
I mean,

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:10.290
even if she stays after and crams,
or whatever,

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:11.790
at this point, it won't do any good.

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:14.080
Akito-kun...

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:17.750
Hang on, Hayama-kun! What are you trying
to do!? Sana-chan is all motivated here!

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:18.750
--Yeah! Yeah!

00:12:18.750 --> 00:12:21.760
Whoo! For the first time in ages,
it's Hard-Boiled Hayama-san!

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:23.760
Hayama-san, this is more like it!

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:25.760
Should we run wild, like we did before?

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:27.100
Hold on, what are you talking about!?

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:30.430
You try anything, and this time,
we're not going to take it sitting down!

00:12:30.430 --> 00:12:32.020
You guys got a lot of nerve!

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:33.020
What did you say!?

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:34.350
What about it!?

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:38.690
Everyone, calm down! A child
who quarrels is a bad child!

00:12:38.690 --> 00:12:40.860
Huh?

00:12:42.700 --> 00:12:44.030
Hayama...

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:47.030
Sana-chan, don't you pay
attention to what Hayama said!

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:49.370
--Yeah! Yeah!

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:50.950
Hayama...

00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:55.750
"Hayama, son, where are you going!?"

00:12:57.380 --> 00:13:00.050
What did you call me
out here to talk about?

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:01.710
Nothing much.

00:13:01.710 --> 00:13:04.050
If you need my advice,
we can talk about anything.

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:07.430
"Yaren 'sodan'..." Just kidding around.

00:13:09.050 --> 00:13:10.060
I- is that...!?

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:11.720
A photograph.

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:15.060
W- what!? But you gave all
the photos back, didn't you!?

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:17.230
There's still one more.

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:22.400
There was one still left in my desk.

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:26.740
Y- you can't... hey, you can't...!
What are you planning to do with that!?

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:30.740
Unless you want it to get out,

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:32.700
you'll do as I say.

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:37.830
Smushed that mosquito!

00:13:46.930 --> 00:13:50.220
Akito-kun! Akito-kun!

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:52.470
Where could Akito-kun have gone?

00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:53.600
Why would he say something
like that all of a sudden?

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:55.930
Why, Hayama!?

00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:58.600
Mitsuya-sensei said you didn't
have any more reason to act out.

00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:00.940
This is lame.

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:03.900
It's lame that all of us have
to stay for after-school class.

00:14:03.940 --> 00:14:06.740
What good will it do for us
to cram for a day or two, at most?

00:14:06.740 --> 00:14:09.620
You can't do what you can't do.

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:10.950
Hayama...

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:12.910
Cut this nonsensical crap out.

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:17.960
Akito-kun is at it again!

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:19.630
"Over the mountains, far to travel,

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:22.290
--people say, happiness dwells.
--I don't want to believe that Akito-kun
is making threats against the teachers,

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:24.590
--"Alas, and I went,
in the crowd of the others,
--like he has done before.

00:14:24.590 --> 00:14:26.970
--and returned with a tear-stained face."
--What do I say to Sana-chan?

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:27.970
"Over the mountains..."

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:29.640
Hayama,

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:31.350
why would you say such a thing?

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:34.890
Hayama, you believed in me,
and yet you said that...

00:14:34.890 --> 00:14:36.890
She can't do anything about her math.

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:40.900
Can't do anything! Can't do anything!
Can't do anything! Can't do anything!

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:43.650
Why did you have to go that far!?

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:44.980
"And so, after school..."

00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:48.240
Look, if you do it this way,
it gets picked up, see?

00:14:48.240 --> 00:14:49.910
Oh, impressive, Aya-chan.

00:14:49.910 --> 00:14:51.570
You're going to make
a good wife for someone.

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:52.910
Don't say that.

00:14:52.910 --> 00:14:57.580
I probably should ask Akito-kun
about this, before I tell Sana-chan...

00:14:57.580 --> 00:15:00.920
But Akito-kun never
listens to what I say.

00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:04.920
Still, I have to say something.
But then what do I do?

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:07.920
Ah, the heart of a
young boy wavers intensely!

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:12.930
Aah, Aya-chan, what should I do!?

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:13.600
Huh?

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:14.930
Tsuyoshi-kun, what's wrong?

00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:19.270
Screaming out someone's name
like that-- it's so embarrassing!

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:20.940
Sana-chan,

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:23.270
I'm going to say it! I'm...

00:15:23.270 --> 00:15:24.940
...going to say it!

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:27.940
Just a minute! Tsuyoshi-kun,
we're in the Mach realm, here!

00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:31.280
Eh!? Hayama has
another make-out picture!?

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:33.530
Shh! Don't say that too loud!

00:15:33.530 --> 00:15:34.870
Oh, sorry.

00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:36.870
But I saw him.

00:15:36.870 --> 00:15:38.160
"Nurse's Office"

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:41.210
Shh! No one can hear!

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:44.540
Sorry. But how could Hayama-kun
do something so extreme again?

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:46.210
It's the truth.

00:15:46.210 --> 00:15:48.590
Put a stop to the
after-school classes and the test.

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:53.220
But why would he be doing this now?

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:57.560
Why are you doing this now, Hayama!?

00:15:57.560 --> 00:15:59.220
Sana-chan, you're going ultra-high speed!

00:15:59.220 --> 00:16:01.560
Hayama!!

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:02.560
What do you want, Kurata?

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:05.230
You should be cleaning the classroom.

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:08.570
You told me you didn't have any more
make-out pictures, but you lied to me!

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:09.900
S- Sana-chan...

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:11.900
--And here I gave you back that
naked photo of you!
--What is she talking about?

00:16:11.900 --> 00:16:13.570
--You're shameless!
--Make-out?

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:15.240
You...

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:18.240
...still have your
indoor uwabaki shoes on.

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:21.040
Make sure you wipe the bottoms of
your shoes when you go back inside.

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:25.580
I can't take it anymore!

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:27.840
What Hayama said is true, though.

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:34.890
I thought you weren't
any good at defense.

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:37.550
Your attack was just too obvious.

00:16:37.550 --> 00:16:39.890
Why, you...! Hold it! Hold it! Hold it!

00:16:39.890 --> 00:16:42.230
--Hold it! Hold it!
--W- what's going on?

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:45.900
Hand over the make-out picture!
Hand it over! Hand it over!!

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:49.900
Once everyone sees that photo...
especially once Andoh-sensei sees it...

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:51.900
We're finished.

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:58.240
There was my name, just now.
Could someone be calling me?

00:16:58.240 --> 00:17:00.580
However, if we can't somehow
persuade Andoh-sensei...

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:01.250
The photo...

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:03.580
Right, he'll show it to everyone,
like he threatened to.

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:05.920
Threatening photo?

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:07.920
This smells like a conspiracy!

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:11.340
"[Conspiracy]--
an evil plan plotted in secret--"

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:09.800
A conspiracy is an evil plan

00:17:09.800 --> 00:17:11.590
that is plotted out in secret.

00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:12.800
A-ha!

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:16.930
Photos? Blackmail?
What exactly is going on!?

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:17.930
Oh, it's just...

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:20.600
Just what!?

00:17:20.600 --> 00:17:22.270
Come on! Tell me!

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:23.270
Well, it's just...

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:26.810
Hand over the
teachers' make-out picture!

00:17:28.270 --> 00:17:31.940
That's our Sana-chan, and her loud voice
training she got from Gekidan Komawari.

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:35.200
Make-out? I know I heard
"make-out picture"!

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:37.200
Make-out picture!

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:39.200
Hand it over! Hand it over!
The teachers making out!

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:42.870
Hold it!

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:44.200
They've been running around
for over ten minutes now.

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:45.210
Amazing.

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:47.870
But what is Kurata
saying about making out?

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:50.540
I know I heard it! "Make-out picture"!

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:54.210
Making out-- teachers, making out!
How disgraceful! How vulgar!

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:58.550
This is beyond serious!

00:17:58.550 --> 00:18:01.890
I know! Now's just
the right time for Burutcha!

00:18:01.890 --> 00:18:03.220
Tackle!

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:05.560
Hayama, why did you go back
to being a bad person!?

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:07.560
You said you didn't
have any more pictures!

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:09.230
You lying, rice-pounding,
desert on the moon!

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:11.570
Shut up! I never told any lies!

00:18:11.570 --> 00:18:13.900
You dummy, dummy, dummy! I'm a
dummy-dummy for believing in you, too!

00:18:13.900 --> 00:18:14.900
Let go of me, would you!?

00:18:14.900 --> 00:18:17.900
Make-out!

00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:21.580
Let me see that picture!

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:22.580
Come on!

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:23.580
I knew it...!

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:26.540
Come on! Come on!

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:31.250
I don't even have it!

00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:39.510
What is this, Tanaka-sensei?

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:41.220
A- actually, I need to talk to you.

00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:45.560
What is it? I was just about to
confirm something very important.

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:48.310
I guess I don't have much choice.
So, what is it?

00:18:49.230 --> 00:18:50.650
It doesn't matter what it is,

00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:53.570
as long as I can change the subject
from the make-out picture...

00:18:53.570 --> 00:18:56.230
R- right! It's about the aptitude test!

00:18:56.230 --> 00:18:57.240
What about it?

00:18:57.240 --> 00:18:58.240
W-well...

00:18:58.240 --> 00:19:00.490
Someone who has been left behind for
years won't be able to do anything

00:19:00.490 --> 00:19:03.200
in just three days.
Testing them won't do any--

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:05.870
That's right! I just remembered!

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:09.000
In short, as educators, our duty should
be to make the subjects understandable,

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:11.540
not to check the students with tests!

00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:14.880
You could say that...
you could say that...!

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:17.880
That is indeed a correct opinion.
But I cannot back off at this point.

00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:19.930
--Please!
--Please!

00:19:19.930 --> 00:19:21.260
Andoh-sensei!

00:19:21.260 --> 00:19:24.220
We want to go to middle school
together with Sana-chan!

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:26.890
If you have to test us,
at least make it a little later!

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:29.560
We will all help take care
of Sana-chan's math!

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:31.270
Oh, you guys...!

00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:32.520
You've got some snot coming out.

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:33.520
--Sensei!
--Sensei!

00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:35.190
--Andoh-sensei!
--Andoh-sensei!

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:38.190
--Sensei!

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:41.860
I- I've become like the
despised teacher in a young adult drama...

00:19:41.860 --> 00:19:45.200
I... I...

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:47.540
Sensei, we love you! Sensei!

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:51.870
Yes, this is ideal education!
This is youth!

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:54.540
I became a teacher in the
hopes of living that scene.

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:56.630
This is bad. This is bad.

00:19:56.630 --> 00:19:58.920
Isn't there some---
isn't there some way out of this?

00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:04.010
I've got a secret plan!

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:03.930
"Complete reversal"

00:20:06.560 --> 00:20:08.310
S- she's on fire...

00:20:09.890 --> 00:20:12.390
Sensei, you see, has actually
just been waiting

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:15.560
to hear those words of friendship
from all of you.

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:18.570
And so, I intentionally took the
role of the hated villain upon me.

00:20:18.570 --> 00:20:21.570
It really was hard on me.

00:20:21.570 --> 00:20:25.240
Everyone, value your friendships.
I will call off the test.

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:26.580
Yay!

00:20:26.580 --> 00:20:28.240
Thank you, Andoh-sensei!

00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:31.250
Wow, I'm saved!

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:34.170
Thank goodness!

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:36.670
--Thank you, Sensei!
--All right, it turned out
the way you wanted.

00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:38.170
Hand over the photo.

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:40.170
Hayama! Don't tell me you...!

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:42.840
Don't tell me you used the
make-out picture for my sake!

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:43.840
Not really.

00:20:43.840 --> 00:20:48.510
Oh, isn't that kind of you!
Still, I'm very happy you did!

00:20:48.510 --> 00:20:52.140
But now, out it out. No more
blackmailing with make-out pictures.

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:55.520
Make-out?

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:56.520
Oh no!

00:20:56.520 --> 00:20:59.860
I know I heard that!
"Make-out pictures"!

00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:00.860
No...!

00:21:00.860 --> 00:21:02.190
It's nothing!

00:21:02.190 --> 00:21:03.530
Yeah! Yeah!

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:05.530
"Making out takes three years,
persimmons eight!"

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:07.820
If you want to see it that bad,
I'll give it to you.

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:18.880
I do indeed have the
make-out picture right here.

00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:19.880
--Hayama!
--Akito-kun!

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:22.380
It wasn't me.
It was the wind. The wind.

00:21:24.220 --> 00:21:26.220
This is...!

00:21:26.220 --> 00:21:30.890
Oh, my! What should I do?
This is so embarrassing...

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:32.890
Limbo dance!?

00:21:32.890 --> 00:21:35.890
Look how pretty it came out!

00:21:35.890 --> 00:21:37.230
--Hayama!
--Akito-kun!

00:21:37.230 --> 00:21:38.560
You tricked us!

00:21:38.560 --> 00:21:41.230
You guys made all that fuss on your own.

00:21:41.230 --> 00:21:43.240
That's right! Limbo!

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:45.700
It's starting to come back to me...
the excitement of that summer...

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:46.570
the exhilaration of that summer...!

00:21:46.570 --> 00:21:48.620
Right now, what children
who are unsure of their futures need

00:21:48.620 --> 00:21:51.240
are memories of those fun days!

00:21:51.240 --> 00:21:55.210
You can use that fun to nurture your
aspirations to become middle-schoolers!

00:21:56.250 --> 00:21:58.250
--L- limbo...

00:21:58.250 --> 00:22:00.920
--Let's limbo!

00:22:00.920 --> 00:22:02.250
--Limbo!

00:22:02.250 --> 00:22:04.760
Let's limbo goes on!

00:22:08.430 --> 00:22:13.390
The students are cheering me on!
This is without question...

00:22:13.390 --> 00:22:15.770
...ideal education!

00:22:15.770 --> 00:22:18.730
Andoh-sensei is going for a new record!

00:22:18.730 --> 00:22:19.730
Let's limbo!

00:22:19.730 --> 00:22:22.070
Do your math, too!

00:22:25.780 --> 00:22:29.740
Here I was worried about things, and came
back in the middle of my business trip,

00:22:29.740 --> 00:22:34.740
but my school is peaceful, peaceful.
It all turned out fine-fine!

00:22:35.410 --> 00:22:40.420
Now I can be with
everyone next year, too!

00:22:40.830 --> 00:22:42.340
"Back against the wall."

00:22:42.840 --> 00:22:47.840
That's what you say about times like these.

00:22:49.090 --> 00:22:52.550
In dire straits,

00:22:53.310 --> 00:22:56.140
I've been waiting for an answer.

00:22:56.640 --> 00:23:00.020
My confessions are worked out
long in advance,

00:23:00.980 --> 00:23:05.110
to always go along with the scenario.

00:23:05.320 --> 00:23:11.160
My heart may be settled, but my mind is in a...

00:23:11.410 --> 00:23:13.370
...panic!!

00:23:14.370 --> 00:23:19.210
When my friends invite me by, suddenly,

00:23:19.410 --> 00:23:21.920
he's there.

00:23:22.830 --> 00:23:25.170
And our usual classroom...

00:23:25.380 --> 00:23:27.760
...quick-changes into a merry-go-round...

00:23:27.840 --> 00:23:30.260
...for two.

00:23:31.090 --> 00:23:33.720
Although I've said nothing but wisecracks...

00:23:33.930 --> 00:23:38.480
...up to now, just for today,

00:23:39.390 --> 00:23:42.060
I'm going to be honest and sincere,

00:23:42.270 --> 00:23:46.780
so BOY, take a look my way!

00:23:47.690 --> 00:23:52.360
When my friends invite me by, suddenly,

00:23:52.530 --> 00:23:55.030
he's there,

00:23:55.990 --> 00:23:58.200
And our usual classroom...

00:23:58.450 --> 00:24:00.790
...quick-changes into a merry-go-round...

00:24:00.910 --> 00:24:03.330
...for two.

00:24:07.050 --> 00:24:10.050
Hoy! In Sana-chan's next adventures...

00:24:10.050 --> 00:24:12.720
They used to say "water spilled returns
not to the basin" a long time ago,

00:24:12.720 --> 00:24:15.720
meaning that you can't put the water back
in the basin once it has spilled out.

00:24:15.720 --> 00:24:17.390
Huh? They still say it now?

00:24:17.390 --> 00:24:19.390
It means that once something is done,
it can't be undone.

00:24:19.390 --> 00:24:22.390
Hayama and Mami-chan... are you two
really water that has spilled now?

00:24:22.390 --> 00:24:24.730
Isn't there any way to get
the water back in the basin?

00:24:24.730 --> 00:24:28.730
Next time on Kodomo no Omocha,
Episode 25, the Sharp Pain in the Chest Saga,

00:24:28.730 --> 00:24:32.400
A Band-Aid For the Heart?

00:24:32.400 --> 00:24:35.410
Just so you know, Babbit is not a rabbit!
